# React 19 — use the new APIs

This app is **React 19** (Vite SPA, no RSC). Prefer the 19 APIs instead of 18-era workarounds. Use them when the situation matches — do not ignore them.

| Situation | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Effect needs a latest callback/prop without retriggering | `useEffectEvent` — **not** `fooRef.current = foo` |
| Hide UI but keep state / skip work offscreen | `<Activity mode="visible" \| "hidden">` |
| Lazy route, async child, or a waiting slot | `<Suspense fallback={...}>` |
| Read a Promise or Context during render | `use()` |
| Pass a ref to a function component | `ref` as a prop — **not** `forwardRef` |

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const onSelectRef = useRef(onSelect);
onSelectRef.current = onSelect;
useEffect(() => {
  map.on("click", (id) => onSelectRef.current(id));
}, []);

// ✅ GOOD
const onSelectEvent = useEffectEvent(onSelect);
useEffect(() => {
  map.on("click", (id) => onSelectEvent(id));
}, []);
```

Still no SSR. Do not add Server Components, `use server`, or `forwardRef`.
